 reconciliation: 'The two statements agree with each other and with the workbook. <strong>WEST = Zones A, C, E and EW = 87,958 modules (52.3 MW)</strong> against the workbook\u2019s contracted quantities of Workforce 35,346 (21.0 MW, Luis\u2019s 20) plus Brumont 53,020 (31.5 MW, Luis\u2019s 30) = 88,366 - a 408-module difference. <strong>EAST = Zones B, D, F and G = 83,512 modules (49.7 MW)</strong> against United\u2019s 50 MW = 84,034 - a 522-module difference. Both sides close to within half a percent.',
 twentyVsFifty: '<strong>The apparent "United 20 MW versus 50 MW" conflict is not a conflict.</strong> 20 MW is United\u2019s RACKING scope - its 497 rows in Zone F carry 35,308 modules, which is 21.0 MW. 50 MW is its MODULE scope, which covers the whole East side including rows that ECCS and Workforce build. Module installation is independent of who racks the row.',
